# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Experiment workflow (mandatory)

Follow `worklog/experiment_SOP.md` for all experiment work. Bookkeeping lives in `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_NN_<name>_claude/` (exp_01 backbone comparison and exp_02 sim-to-real are retrospective records; exp_03 yaw rotation is the first SOP-native experiment). Roles (per Yixun 2026-09-15): Planner = main session (Claude Fable 5.1); **Coder = Claude Opus 5** (Agent tool model `opus`, max effort, working in the experiment's git worktree `/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code_wt`); **code Reviewer = OpenAI Codex `gpt-6-astra` at Ultra** (`codex exec -s read-only -C <worktree> --skip-git-repo-check "<prompt>" < /dev/null`; stdin must be closed; the config `~/.codex/config.toml` sets the model; the final message is saved as the review with the identity header); plan reviews stay with Codex. From 2026-09-12 to 2026-09-15 the Coder was Codex (`codex exec -s workspace-write …`) and the code Reviewer a Fable subagent (exp_05 rounds, exp_06 round 1); before 2026-09-12 the Coder was an Opus subagent and Codex reviewed code (exp_03 and the exp_04 plan reviews ran on `gpt-5.6-sol`, as their headers say). Save every review with the identity header; log every action in the experiment's `_worklog.md`.

## Repo overview

Unofficial implementation of **xRIR** (CVPR 2025, "Hearing Anywhere in Any Environment"): predict a single-channel room impulse response (RIR) for a query source/receiver pair from a panoramic depth map at the receiver, conditioned on a few-shot support set of measured RIRs from the same room. Data is the Treble-simulated **AcousticRooms** dataset.

The active research question is a **receiver-frame / coordinate-convention ablation** of the baseline. It lives on branches (see "Branches and current experiment"). This CLAUDE.md is gitignored and shared across all checkouts, so run `git branch --show-current` and read `plans/xRIR_v0.md` before assuming which experiment is in play.

## Environment and data

- Use the `xRIR` conda env (Python 3.8, torch 2.0.1+cu117, numpy 1.23). It matches `requirements.txt`. The `base` env is Python 3.13 / torch 2.7 and is **not** compatible.
- Always set `PYTHONPATH` to the repo root; scripts use bare `from model...` / `from utils...` imports:

```bash
conda activate xRIR
export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:$(pwd)
```

- Datasets read from `XRIR_DATA_PATH` if set, else `./data/`. Locally `data/{single_channel_ir,depth_map,metadata}` are symlinks into a CIFS network share (`/media/diskstation/...`); never write into them. That share is far too slow for training: every sample does a 1600-entry `os.listdir` plus ~20 small reads, and 32 loader workers stalled it completely. A local NVMe mirror lives at `/home/yixunhu/data_cache/AcousticRooms/{single_channel_ir,depth_map,metadata}` (~33 GB); run anything heavier than a smoke test with `XRIR_DATA_PATH=/home/yixunhu/data_cache/AcousticRooms`.
- Pretrained checkpoints (gitignored, present locally): `checkpoints/xRIR_unseen.pth`, `checkpoints/xRIR_seen.pth`. The seen checkpoint was saved from `DataParallel`, so `eval_seen.py` strips the `module.` prefix.
- `train_xRIR_unseen.py` saves to `./ckpt/xRIR_{num_shot}_shot/`; `torch.save` does not create directories, so `mkdir -p` it first.

## Common commands

```bash
# Original scripts (no argparse; hyperparams, checkpoint paths and num_shot live in __main__)
python eval_unseen.py          # 8-shot, unseen-room test split, loads checkpoints/xRIR_unseen.pth
